# Flutter Development Standards

## State Management
- Use Provider for state management
- Keep state close to where it's used
- Use immutable state objects
- Implement appropriate state update mechanisms

## Widget Guidelines
- Break down large widgets into smaller, reusable components
- Use const constructors whenever possible
- Implement proper widget lifecycle methods
- Use keys appropriately for widget identification

## Performance
- Use const widgets for static content
- Implement proper widget disposal
- Use ListView.builder for long lists
- Cache expensive computations

## Error Handling
- Use try-catch blocks for async operations
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Log errors appropriately

## Testing
- Write unit tests for business logic
- Write widget tests for UI components
- Write integration tests for critical flows
- Maintain good test coverage

## Development Tools
- Cursor: Code editing
- Flutter analysis tools: Code analysis
- Performance analysis tools: Performance optimization
- Code formatting tools: Code standardization





